    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43779.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "This is the Daily Blast from the New Republic, produced and presented by the DSR Network. I'm your host, Greg Sargent. Here on the podcast, we repeatedly argued that Mike Johnson might ultimately allow a vote on military aid to Ukraine, even if this puts him at risk of getting ousted as speaker by MAGA forces in the House. Well, we're glad to see that this is now coming to pass. The House GOP leadership is now preparing to move forward with the Ukraine aid as part of a broader set of bills, and predictably, Representative Marjorie Taylor Greene is furious. Why is Johnson doing this now, and what are the prospects for success? To unravel all this, today we're talking to Democratic Representative Mikey Sherrill of New Jersey, a former U.S. Navy pilot and member of the Armed Services Committee. Welcome, Congresswoman.",
