  {
    "episode_id": 43779,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43779.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "So here's what we know so far. Mike Johnson appears prepared to move four bills, one funding Ukraine, one on Israel, one on Taiwan, and one more with a grab bag of goodies that are supposed to make right-wing Republicans happy. There are some indications that the funding levels will potentially match the bill that passed the Senate on a broad bipartisan basis, 60 billion for Ukraine, 14 billion for Israel. What's your reaction to this bill? Are those measures aside from the last one, of course, things that a lot of House Democrats are going to be able to support?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
