    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43779.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think you know what I haven't heard yet is what the funding for humanitarian aid for Gaza will look like, and that is critical to Democrats. So I don't know that there's any moving forward without that important aid for most Democrats. But that said, this does seem to be largely in line with the supplemental And so I think Democrats will support it with the understanding of how critical it is to get aid to Ukraine very, very quickly. Again, that said, it does beg the question, why aren't we just passing the Senate supplemental, which was so bipartisan, 70 votes, could get on the president's desk almost immediately and get the aid there as quickly as possible. The concern here, I believe the Senate's out of session next week. And with their procedures, this could take some time to get through the Senate. And I'm not sure anybody's whipped the votes there as to how they will feel about it. And we really can't until we see the text.",
