    "turn_text": "Yeah, I think the Ukraine aid seems to have wide support. You know, once ago it was at about 300 votes, I think. So I would assume that right now we still have wide ranging support for that. In fact, at a House Armed Services Committee hearing, I was at several weeks ago when it came up, the chairman was quick to remind people that he was a strong supporter of Ukrainian aid. It's my understanding that other committee chairs in this sort of foreign policy national security intelligence space are very much in favor of Ukrainian aid. When I was over in Munich, I know several of the Republicans were very strongly in support of Ukrainian aid. So it does seem as if we'll have the votes on both the Democratic and Republican side to get the Ukrainian aid support we need.",
