  {
    "episode_id": 43779,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43779.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "It does look that way, and it looks like Johnson is listening to some of those really highly influential Republican committee chairs, which is a dynamic that I think has been lost on a lot of people. It's pretty striking. One question here for Democrats is whether they can trust that Johnson actually will hold a vote on Ukraine, aid if Dems supply votes to move ahead with a rule. My sense from talking to Dems, and I want to see what you think of this, is that they see Johnson's personal word as more trustworthy than that of former Speaker Kevin McCarthy. Is that your view? And do you have any doubts that Johnson would stick to his word if he pledged to hold a vote on money for Ukraine?",
