    "turn_text": "Yes, Johnson is more credible than Speaker McCarthy. I think that's a pretty little bar, however. So, you know, understanding what kind of commitment we have. I, you know, as we move forward with the rule, I would prefer, and I've expressed this to my leadership, that once these bills are on the floor, that the Ukrainian bill, aid bill come first, that would give me some sense of confidence as we move through As he seems to want to do breaking up the bills. I've not received assurances that will be the case. So again, I think largely what we're working on now is understanding the substance of these bills and what will be in them. And yes, there was some sense there'd be aid, but, but I'm concerned about. what that aid looks like and the amount of the aid that we'd see and that's really critical. So I have had conversations with my leadership about how once the rules passed and the votes are on the floor, I would like to see that Ukrainian vote come up first before we work through the other ones.",
