    "turn_text": "It certainly does seem like the presence is robust. I do want to ask you something else about some of these mega-friendly lawmakers. Some of them, like JD Vance, have purported to offer a more serious argument, at least according to them, against Ukraine aid than, say, whatever green says. So people like Vance will say our aid won't make enough of a difference on the numbers. And they'll say Biden hasn't told us what the plan for Ukrainian victory is. I wanted to get your response to those claims, but also I'm curious to know whether lawmakers like Vance actually get briefings from our intelligence agencies and others in the administration that have answered those questions. I would think you would have seen some of those briefings. And it just struck me from Vance's New York Times op-ed that Surely he's had a chance to raise these concerns with people who have answers to them. Your take on all that?",
